;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; name: lobby-profile.gc
;; name in dgo: lobby-profile
;; dgos: MENU2

;; DECOMP BEGINS

;; issue 699 rung 3b (reprioritized by issue 759 to make the profile screen
;; the port's first visible menu): scoped decode of lobby-profile, this
;; worktree's own decompiler/config (scratch --proj-path, allowed_objects
;; ["lobby-profile"]; the worktree's own out/jakx/fr3/GAME.fr3 is untouched,
;; verified byte-identical before and after). lobby-profile.o owns
;; lobby-menu-manager's states 125-140 plus 162 (autosave-icon, outside the
;; old menu-road survey's stated 125-140 range but installed by this same
;; object; discovered from this rung's own scoped decode, not guessed).
;;
;; All fifteen numbered slots' real retail names came from this decode's own
;; "Disagreement between state name and type system name" errors against
;; the placeholder :state-methods entries; renamed both
;; decompiler/config/jakx/all-types.gc and goal_src/jakx/engine/net/lobby-
;; menu-manager-h.gc to the real names (125 new-load-profile, 126 load-
;; profile, 127 loading-profile, 129 enter-profile-name, 130 save-profile,
;; 131 no-card, 132 want-format, 133 formating-card, 134 want-create-file,
;; 135 creating-file, 136 select-save-profile, 137 overwrite-profile, 138
;; saving-profile, 139 new-load-save-profile, 140 boot-memory-card, 162
;; autosave-icon) before redecoding, the same class of rename rung 3's own
;; waiting-for-cd/pre-game-type-menu landing used. Every one of these
;; fifteen states installs via a raw top-level (new 'static 'state ...)
;; literal plus (method-set! lobby-menu-manager <slot> ...), never a bare
;; defstate the decompiler can auto-detect on its own - matching this
;; corpus's own "'global state installs" idiom (lobby-net-startup.gc); once
;; the type's own slot name matches the state's own :name field, the
;; decompiler emits a normal defstate wrapper around that same install, and
;; every state below is transcribed from that clean defstate output.
;;
;; TIER 1, landed for real (this rung's own acceptance bar - issue 759's
;; "profile screen becomes the first visible menu"): boot-memory-card (140,
;; the memory-card status gate lobby-net-startup.gc's own pre-game-type-menu
;; go-virtuals into unconditionally on a fresh cold boot) and new-load-
;; profile (125, the real first screen: a two-row "New Profile"/"Load
;; Profile" side-bar, boot-memory-card's own unconditional fallback
;; destination on a normal boot with a readable card - traced end to end,
;; see the marker census in the PR/issue thread). new-load-save-profile
;; (139, the same side-bar reached later from game-type-menu's own 'profile
;; selection, not from a cold boot) is landed alongside it since its own
;; :event/:exit/:trans decoded clean and its :enter needed only the same
;; mechanical fixup as new-load-profile's.
;;
;; Two decompiler-only notation classes needed manual resolution, both
;; confirmed by direct compilation rather than by reading dead text (menu2-
;; draw.gc's own header lists the general doctrine this rung follows):
;; raw offset math needs an int/float base (basic/none-typed bases are
;; wrapped (the-as int ...) at the point of use), and (call!)/(ret-value
;; ...)/(ret-none) are decompiler bookkeeping rewritten to a direct call
;; through the loaded t9-N register and the bare trailing return form.
;; boot-memory-card's :code and every TIER 1 state's own :enter share one
;; more recurring class not previously named in this corpus: a "is this
;; menu-info's base-menu already one of my own open children" guard, a
;; dotimes over (+ (-> self in-focus-index) 1) reading (-> self menu-handles
;; i), converting each live handle to its process, casting (the-as base-menu
;; ...), and comparing -> info-ptr against the menu-info global by pointer
;; identity - the decoder always leaves this raw ((l.wu (+ a0 248)) against
;; a none-typed base, "Could not figure out load"), never resolving that a0
;; is (the-as base-menu process) and 248 is base-menu's own info-ptr field
;; under the all-types N+4 basic-load convention (child-handles 248,
;; info-ptr 252). Written below as the same dotimes/(return #f) idiom
;; (method 186 lobby-menu-manager, already landed above in lobby-menu-
;; manager.gc, uses the identical "dotimes over menu-handles, return early"
;; shape), not the raw goto/label soup the decoder itself emits, except in
;; boot-memory-card's :code where the scan sits inside a cond TEST (not the
;; whole function) and an early function-wide return would change behavior;
;; there it keeps an explicit goto/label pair matching this file's own
;; inspect methods' established use of the same construct.
;;
;; *menu-new-load-profile*'s own :children tree (a 'selection-menu-manager
;; wrapper over two dropdown-item-info rows, 3d-menu-type "skel-side-bar" -
;; matching issue 699's own screenshot survey exactly) is transcribed field-
;; for-field from this decode's own raw word dump, cross-checked against
;; decompiler/config/jakx/all-types.gc's own base-menu-info/sprite-menu-
;; info/string-menu-info/dropdown-item-info/animation-info/transition-info/
;; dropdown-trans-info/string-info offset-assert layouts (all already
;; landed there), the same non-guessed method lobby-menu-data.gc's own
;; *base-menu-info* citation used. label_types.jsonc gained a "lobby-
;; profile" hint section (ten top-level labels, base-menu-info) so the top
;; level of all ten *menu-*-profile* globals decodes as real fields rather
;; than <static-data LXXX>; label_types.jsonc hints do not reach nested
;; boxed-array elements (lobby-menu-data.gc's own *base-menu-info* citation
;; already documents this), so *menu-new-load-profile*'s own nested
;; children (the two dropdown-item-info rows and their own trans-info/
;; strings-info) are hand-traced from the raw word dump instead, the same
;; method that citation used, since that tree alone feeds TIER 1's
;; acceptance bar. *menu-new-load-save-profile* and *menu-boot-
;; memorycard* keep their own children at the decoder's own one-level-deep
;; placeholder (a real, non-#f pointer the decoder itself cannot yet type
;; further); not chased this rung since neither sits on the TIER 1 boot
;; path (new-load-save-profile's own tree is reached only from game-type-
;; menu's 'profile branch, already landed above; boot-memory-card's own
;; child is a profile-yes-no-string prompt, the rare missing/slow-card
;; branch, not the default advance).
;;
;; TIER 2, held (issue 699's own "memory-card screens", not this rung's
;; stated acceptance bar): load-profile, loading-profile, enter-profile-
;; name, save-profile, no-card, want-format, want-create-file, formating-
;; card, creating-file, overwrite-profile, saving-profile, select-save-
;; profile and autosave-icon all decode (their :event/:trans handlers call
;; two functions, go-profile-state and memcard-continue, that this decode's
;; own "function has no type analysis. Cannot decompile" marks the same
;; cannot-decompile class as menu-clear-strip - a real defun each, hand-
;; wrappable around raw register writes, but not attempted this rung), and
;; dropdown-profile/title-load-save-profile/profile-error-string/profile-
;; yes-no-string/profile-loading-string (the widget classes those held
;; states spawn) decode with their own per-field type-prop errors on top.
;; None of the thirteen had ever been installed by any defstate or method-
;; set! anywhere in the corpus (same "raw 0 slips through the #f-only
;; dispatch guard" class issue 699's own road audit already documents for
;; ~30 other slots elsewhere on this type), so landing them here as the
;; same minimal inert park is a strict improvement (crash -> park), not a
;; new hazard, and does not touch this rung's own cold-boot acceptance
;; path: nothing TIER 1 lands go-virtuals into a TIER 2 slot except on
;; explicit player input past the first screen (selecting new/load profile
;; and completing that flow), the same rung-boundary shape every other
;; partially-landed menu branch in this corpus already has.

;; definition for symbol *profile-errors-continue*, type object
(define *profile-errors-continue* (the-as object (new 'static 'boxed-array :type uint32 #x9a #x9c #x9e)))

;; definition for symbol *profile-yes-no*, type object
(define *profile-yes-no* (the-as object (new 'static 'boxed-array :type uint32 #x9a #x9c #x9e #xb59)))

;; definition for symbol *profile-not-remove*, type array
(define *profile-not-remove* (the-as array (new 'static 'boxed-array :type uint32 #x9a #x9c #x9e)))

;; definition for symbol *profile-load-save-ids*, type array
(define *profile-load-save-ids* (the-as array (new 'static 'boxed-array :type uint32 #x2e)))

;; definition for symbol *menu-new-load-profile*, type object
;; issue 699 rung 3b / issue 759: the real first screen's own info block, a
;; two-row "New Profile"/"Load Profile" side-bar. :children traced two
;; levels deep per this file's own header note above; the "skel-side-bar"
;; 3d-menu-type string and the two dropdown-item-info rows' :selection-type
;; symbols ('new-profile, 'load-profile) are the direct evidence this is
;; issue 699's own screenshot survey's first screen. string-info's own
;; :pos-z value (#xffff010) is transcribed as the literal raw word the
;; decode gives; nothing in this rung's own scope reads or explains it
;; further.
(define *menu-new-load-profile*
  (the-as object (new 'static 'base-menu-info
                   :menu-type 'base-menu
                   :children (new 'static 'boxed-array :type base-menu-info
                     (new 'static 'base-menu-info
                       :menu-type 'selection-menu-manager
                       :children (new 'static 'boxed-array :type dropdown-item-info
                         (new 'static 'dropdown-item-info
                           :menu-type 'dropdown-item
                           :children #f
                           :name-symbol #f
                           :3d-menu-type #f
                           :trans-info (new 'static 'dropdown-trans-info
                             :enter-anim -1
                             :exit-anim -1
                             :running-anim -1
                             :anim-speed 5.0
                             :enter-delay 0
                             :3d-offset (new 'static 'vector :data (new 'static 'array float 4 0.0 -6144.0 0.0 1.0))
                             :enter-pos-x 0.0
                             :enter-pos-y 0.0
                             :enter-alpha 1.0
                             :running-alpha 1.0
                             :exit-alpha 1.0
                             :running-pos-x 0.0
                             :running-pos-y 0.0
                             :exit-pos-x 0.0
                             :exit-pos-y 0.0
                             :move-rate 100.0
                             :scroll-offset-x 0
                             :scroll-offset-y 0
                             :scroll-rate 0.0
                             )
                           :joint-index -1
                           :joint-index-2 -1
                           :box-index 0
                           :joints #f
                           :width -1
                           :height #x1000
                           :scale-y 1.0
                           :scale-x 1.0
                           :sprites-info #f
                           :color 0
                           :strings-info (new 'static 'boxed-array :type string-info
                             (new 'static 'string-info
                               :offset-x 0.0
                               :offset-y 0.0
                               :offset-z -1.0
                               :offset-w 1.0
                               :pos-z #xffff010
                               :id #x32
                               :font-scale 0.5
                               :width -1.0
                               :height -1.0
                               :string-ptr #f
                               :string-ptr-needs-format #t
                               :font-flags #x122e
                               :font-color #x34
                               :font-color-2 #x33
                               :font-color-3 6
                               :offset-dir 2
                               :offset-from-index -1
                               :offset-type-from 0
                               :is-player-string #f
                               :tmp-talking 0
                               :extra-arg #f
                               )
                             )
                           :text-ids #f
                           :selection-box-width -1
                           :selection-box-height -1
                           :selection-type 'new-profile
                           :selection-extra 0
                           :selection-box-offset (new 'static 'vector :data (new 'static 'array float 4 0.0 0.0 0.0 1.0))
                           :selection-box-color #x30400020
                           :down-index-modifier 1
                           :up-index-modifier -1
                           :left-index-modifier 0
                           :right-index-modifier 0
                           :selection-box-texture-index 7
                           :reset-pad 1
                           )
                         (new 'static 'dropdown-item-info
                           :menu-type 'dropdown-item
                           :children #f
                           :name-symbol #f
                           :3d-menu-type #f
                           :trans-info (new 'static 'dropdown-trans-info
                             :enter-anim -1
                             :exit-anim -1
                             :running-anim -1
                             :anim-speed 5.0
                             :enter-delay 0
                             :3d-offset (new 'static 'vector :data (new 'static 'array float 4 0.0 -10240.0 0.0 1.0))
                             :enter-pos-x 0.0
                             :enter-pos-y 0.0
                             :enter-alpha 1.0
                             :running-alpha 1.0
                             :exit-alpha 1.0
                             :running-pos-x 0.0
                             :running-pos-y 0.0
                             :exit-pos-x 0.0
                             :exit-pos-y 0.0
                             :move-rate 100.0
                             :scroll-offset-x 0
                             :scroll-offset-y 0
                             :scroll-rate 0.0
                             )
                           :joint-index -1
                           :joint-index-2 -1
                           :box-index 0
                           :joints #f
                           :width -1
                           :height #x1000
                           :scale-y 1.0
                           :scale-x 1.0
                           :sprites-info #f
                           :color 0
                           :strings-info (new 'static 'boxed-array :type string-info
                             (new 'static 'string-info
                               :offset-x 0.0
                               :offset-y 0.0
                               :offset-z -1.0
                               :offset-w 1.0
                               :pos-z #xffff010
                               :id #x2e
                               :font-scale 0.5
                               :width -1.0
                               :height -1.0
                               :string-ptr #f
                               :string-ptr-needs-format #t
                               :font-flags #x122e
                               :font-color #x34
                               :font-color-2 #x33
                               :font-color-3 6
                               :offset-dir 2
                               :offset-from-index -1
                               :offset-type-from 0
